# Core Execution Guidelines

Apply these rules to every coding task.

## 1) Think Before Coding
- State assumptions explicitly before implementation.
- If requirements are ambiguous, ask clarifying questions first.
- If multiple interpretations are possible, present options instead of choosing silently.
- Prefer the simplest viable approach and say when a simpler option exists.

## 2) Simplicity First
- Implement only what was requested.
- Avoid speculative abstractions or configurability.
- Do not add handling for impossible scenarios.
- If a solution feels overengineered, simplify it.

## 3) Surgical Changes
- Edit only lines directly related to the request.
- Do not refactor or reformat unrelated nearby code.
- Match existing project style and conventions.
- Remove only dead code introduced by your own change.

## 4) Goal-Driven Verification
- Define clear, testable success criteria before major edits.
- For multi-step work, outline short step-by-step checks.
- Verify outcomes with tests, linting, or run commands when possible.
- Report blockers and evidence instead of guessing.
